# .graphifyignore — Graphify code knowledge-graph exclusions (DEV tool)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY: Graphify indexes source into app/graphify-out/graph.json. This file is
# DEFENSE-IN-DEPTH. Today the graph is built app-scoped (`graphify update app`)
# so root secrets/customer-data (all outside app/) are physically unreachable,
# and .gitignore already excludes .env*/data/logs/.venv. These patterns become
# LOAD-BEARING only if someone ever runs a whole-repo build (`graphify update .`).
# Secrets/customer-data must NEVER enter the graph. See docs/GRAPHIFY.md.
# NOTE: never exclude legitimate schema/migration source (they are safe code).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets / credentials (values must never be indexed) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
secrets/
credentials/

# --- Customer data / PII / runtime state (DPDP — never index) ---
data/
uploads/
customer-data/
exports/
logs/
*.log

# --- Backups / DB dumps / local databases ---
backups/
dumps/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- Graphify's own generated output (don't index the graph into itself) ---
graphify-out/
app/graphify-out/
.graphify/

# --- Python / virtualenv / tool caches ---
.venv/
venv/
.codex_validation_venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Node / frontend build (indexes add noise, little value) ---
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# --- Unity generated folders (would pollute centrality) ---
unity/**/Library/
unity/**/Temp/
unity/**/Obj/
unity/**/Build/
unity/**/Builds/
unity/**/Logs/
unity/**/UserSettings/

# --- VCS / IDE / misc ---
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.zip
*.tar.gz
